  "description": "The Supernought has been in the wild long enough to earn its name. It’s not a concept and it’s not here to be everything. It’s a dedicated downhill performance bike, refined around a single purpose: carrying more speed, with more control, in the roughest places you can point it.\n\nPair our most refined high pivot layout with 205mm of rear travel and the result is simple. The Supernought stays calm when the track turns violent. It carries momentum through roots, square edges, and braking bumps. It holds a line when the ground is trying to deflect you, and it keeps the bike working underneath you instead of reacting on top of it.\n\nWhat happens next is on you. You brake later. You commit sooner. You choose lines that used to feel like a bad idea, then ride out the other side with a grin. No fluff. No filler. No compromises. Supernought.\n\nThe Supernought has been in the wild long enough to earn its name. It’s not a concept and it’s not here to be everything. It’s a dedicated downhill performance bike, refined around a single purpose: carrying more speed, with more control, in the roughest places you can point it.\n\nPair our most refined high pivot layout with 205mm of rear travel and the result is simple. The Supernought stays calm when the track turns violent. It carries momentum through roots, square edges, and braking bumps. It holds a line when the ground is trying to deflect you, and it keeps the bike working underneath you instead of reacting on top of it.\n\nWhat happens next is on you. You brake later. You commit sooner. You choose lines that used to feel like a bad idea, then ride out the other side with a grin. No fluff. No filler. No compromises. Supernought.",
